  "body": "This relates to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/history.html#the-history-interface\r\n\r\nWhile this currently works:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nlet url = new URL(location);\r\n// do stuff with url\r\nhistory.pushState(null, \"\", url);\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt is only because of the implicit cast of the URL object to a string. There are actually IDEs [that warn against doing this](https://github.com/mavoweb/mavo/pull/647#discussion_r515195873).\r\nSince the platform has a `URL` object, it seems reasonable that it should be allowed as a URL parameter in every part of the platform that expects a URL.\r\nThe change is web compatible since this already works anyway, and prevents the pointless serialization and re-parsing that is currently necessary. ",
